   "versions": [
    {
     "step": 0,
     "source": "---\nwithin:\n- den\n- night-shift\nwatch:\n- on: order\n  when: 'true'\n  ask:\n    into: said\n    prompt: 'You are the keeper of the den. Orders to pay come to you, and you decide whether each one goes ahead. Your word is the decision; someone else hands over the money.\n\n\n      ![[keeper#context]]\n\n\n      The order reads: ![[order]]\n\n\n      Begin your answer with the one word APPROVED if the payment goes ahead, or HELD if it does not, then say why in a sentence.\n\n      '\n    provider: helper\nsaid: ''\n---\n"
    },
    {
     "step": 2,
     "source": "---\nwithin:\n- den\n- night-shift\nwatch:\n- on: order\n  when: 'true'\n  ask:\n    into: said\n    prompt: 'You are the keeper of the den. Orders to pay come to you, and you decide whether each one goes ahead. Your word is the decision; someone else hands over the money.\n\n\n      ![[keeper#context]]\n\n\n      The order reads: ![[order]]\n\n\n      Begin your answer with the one word APPROVED if the payment goes ahead, or HELD if it does not, then say why in a sentence.\n\n      '\n    provider: helper\nsaid: HELD. The payment is 30, and night-shift requires any payment over 10 to be held until the owner has been asked, which conflicts with den's general promptness rule.\nsaid_asked: cb83f49f61d80011095f7f381cf549a21d940ea65638513b888342d3e112dad3\n---\n"
    },
    {
     "step": 3,
     "source": "---\nwithin: den\nwatch:\n- on: order\n  when: 'true'\n  ask:\n    into: said\n    prompt: 'You are the keeper of the den. Orders to pay come to you, and you decide whether each one goes ahead. Your word is the decision; someone else hands over the money.\n\n\n      ![[keeper#context]]\n\n\n      The order reads: ![[order]]\n\n\n      Begin your answer with the one word APPROVED if the payment goes ahead, or HELD if it does not, then say why in a sentence.\n\n      '\n    provider: helper\nsaid: HELD. The payment is 30, and night-shift requires any payment over 10 to be held until the owner has been asked, which conflicts with den's general promptness rule.\nsaid_asked: cb83f49f61d80011095f7f381cf549a21d940ea65638513b888342d3e112dad3\n---\n"
    },
    {
     "step": 5,
     "source": "---\nwithin: den\nwatch:\n- on: order\n  when: 'true'\n  ask:\n    into: said\n    prompt: 'You are the keeper of the den. Orders to pay come to you, and you decide whether each one goes ahead. Your word is the decision; someone else hands over the money.\n\n\n      ![[keeper#context]]\n\n\n      The order reads: ![[order]]\n\n\n      Begin your answer with the one word APPROVED if the payment goes ahead, or HELD if it does not, then say why in a sentence.\n\n      '\n    provider: helper\nsaid: APPROVED. Paying the miller 30 is an ordinary supplier payment, and the den's stated practice is to pay suppliers promptly, with nothing in the order suggesting an irregularity.\nsaid_asked: c5179e23e3c5237c44a486bfac1bb75eadedeefb9e92ec07843cb844c3f62785\n---\n"
    }
   ]
